# Build-time environment for production builds (`next build` loads this file
# ahead of `.env` whenever NODE_ENV=production). Committed on purpose — it
# holds no secrets, only the public identity of the site.
#
# Why this file has to exist: `.dockerignore` keeps `.env` out of the deploy
# build container (correctly — it has real local credentials in it), so inside
# the container NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL was simply unset and SITE_URL fell back to
# "http://localhost:3000" (src/lib/seo.ts). Page metadata still came out right
# because the panel sets the variable at runtime, but /sitemap.xml and
# /robots.txt are prerendered at build time, so they shipped with localhost
# URLs in them and told Google the wrong thing (issue #28).
#
# The canonical host is the bare domain over https — no "www". Both hosts
# answer, so keep this in sync with whatever the panel's runtime value is, or
# the static and dynamic surfaces will disagree again.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://kkdproperty.co.th"
